    "lawCode": "Add Art 130 Subart 5 §6518, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6717\n\nSPONSOR: STAVISKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to allowing for a certain\namount of required clinical training and competency to be completed\nthrough simulation experience\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow for professions under the purview of this title to complete at\nleast one-third of their clinical training through simulation experi-\nences.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection One allows for postsecondary institutions, offering professional\nlicensure education programs for professions under this title, the abil-\nity to offer at least one-third of clinical training through simulation\nexperiences. Additionally, the bill notes that postsecondary insti-\ntutions may provide more than one-third of clinical training as simu-\nlation experiences such that an application is provided to the Depart-\nment of Education.\n\nSection Two notes the effective date of this legislation.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill allows postsecondary institutions to provide more flexible\nmethods of the delivery of clinical experiences for professional licen-\nsure education programs and helps modernized education programs to\naccount for new technological methods of curriculum delivery. Addi-\ntionally, the bill provides students in professional licensure education\nprograms greater flexibility in earning clinical experience hours.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect 180 days after it shall have become law.\n",
