    "lawCode": "Amd §§6905, 6906 & 6910, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6717A\n\nSPONSOR: STAVISKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to allowing for a certain\namount of required clinical training and competency for licensing as a\nregistered professional nurse, licensed practical nurse, and nurse prac-\ntitioner to be completed through simulation experience\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow for nursing professions to complete at least one-third of their\nclinical training through simulation experiences.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 allows for postsecondary institutions, offering professional\nlicensure education programs for the three nursing titles; RNs, LPNs,\nand NPs, the ability to offer at least one-third of clinical training\nthrough simulation experiences. Additionally, the bill notes that post-\nsecondary institutions may provide more than one-third of clinical\ntraining as simulation experiences such that an application is provided\nto the Department of Education.\n\nSection 2 notes the effective date of this legislation.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill allows postsecondary institutions to provide more flexible\nmethods of the delivery of clinical experiences for nursing licensure\neducation programs and helps modernized education programs to account\nfor new technological methods of curriculum delivery.  Additionally, the\nbill provides nursing students in licensure education programs greater\nflexibility in earning clinical experience hours.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect 180 days after it shall have become law.\n",
